    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI IC vote eval\nThe AI IC project posts its vote and ratings here. n8n answers 202 at once, then GitHub Actions (score-vote.yml) runs the eval and posts the result back to the Wait node. Only failures go to Slack. A vote that passes posts nothing.\n\n**Credentials to create (by name):**\n1. `AI IC Vote Webhook Auth` (Header Auth: header `X-Eval-Token`) on the Webhook node. The skill sends this value.\n2. `Eval Result Webhook Auth` (Header Auth: header `X-Eval-Token`) on the Wait node. Use the same value as the GitHub secret `EVAL_RESULT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN`.\n3. `GitHub - Dispatch Token` (Header Auth: `Authorization` = `Bearer <token>`, permission to run workflows on the repo) on `GitHub: Score Vote`.\n4. `Slack account` (Slack API) on the three Slack nodes, and set the channel in each.\n\n**Import steps:**\n1. Import this file and attach each credential above.\n2. Set `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL` in the three Slack nodes.\n3. Activate the workflow and put its production webhook URL in the skill.\n\n**Timeout:** the Wait node runs for 3 minutes. When the limit is reached, n8n resumes the run on the normal output with no body. `Eval: Read Result` sees no `exit_code`, and `IF: Eval Finished` sends the run to `Slack: Eval Did Not Finish`.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 560
      },
